                        "form_id": "2b35e2ac-edfb-4286-a5c5-24f70d506dd0",
                        "entry_id": "abfbeeed-23f8-34f1-9107-f89907386e04",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "bryophytes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f7d099f5-0ea4-3e64-bc51-abe972ca74ff",
                        "entry_id": "abfbeeed-23f8-34f1-9107-f89907386e04",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Plante terrestre de la famille des Bryophyta, caractérisée par l’absence de vrai système vasculaire : ce sont des plantes qui résistent à la dessiccation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d33fbb36-ec0c-4d06-9b6b-61f897a1af84",
                                "sense_id": "f7d099f5-0ea4-3e64-bc51-abe972ca74ff",
                                "text": "Les “vols de bombardes” continuent en canopée et, en sous-bois, nos commençons les récoltes de bryophytes, hépatiques et mousses ; ces groupes peu étudiés sont d’une diversité inattendue."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4b0d6c3f-d240-4fb7-b8e2-3d239dc063cb",
                                "sense_id": "f7d099f5-0ea4-3e64-bc51-abe972ca74ff",
                                "text": "Il faut souligner que le massif vosgien, plus précisément le Val-de-Senones, constitue pour beaucoup de botanistes un véritable spot en matière de biodiversité pour les ptéridophytes et les bryophytes […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3148f5f9-0ba4-4449-a840-32c264676e8e",
                                "sense_id": "f7d099f5-0ea4-3e64-bc51-abe972ca74ff",
                                "text": "En raison de l’épaisse couche de feuilles mortes qui recouvre le sol de la Hêtraie, les Bryophytes —réserve faite des espèces corticoles— se font rares […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0ae0468d-73b3-4955-9927-cbf981389a3b",
                        "source_entry_id": "abfbeeed-23f8-34f1-9107-f89907386e04",
                        "source_sense_id": "f7d099f5-0ea4-3e64-bc51-abe972ca74ff",
                        "target_lang_word": "bryophyte",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bryophyte",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e7609cd2-202e-38df-a35a-bb737591908b",
                                        "entry_id": "4d451108-5a5c-3319-8ab8-51aa3c4d7617",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any plant of the division Bryophyta, defined sensu lato to comprise the mosses, liverworts and hornworts and corresponding to all embryophytes that are not vascular plants."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea9ee9ed-e7b7-4d87-ae4a-7129d75446d3",
                                                "sense_id": "e7609cd2-202e-38df-a35a-bb737591908b",
                                                "text": "Without going into their reasons, Bold, Alexopoulos, & DelBevoryas (1980) and Crandall-Stotler (1980) believe that there are at least three independent lines of bryophytes and that this is best reflected by establishing three divisions - the Bryophyta (mosses), Hepatophyta (liverworts), and Anthocerotophyta (hornworts)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b6ad3878-fc54-43c4-8843-8fb6b08c1ab4",
                                                "sense_id": "e7609cd2-202e-38df-a35a-bb737591908b",
                                                "text": "2002, William R. Buck, Bryophytes, entry in Niles Eldredge (editor), Life on Earth, page 202,\nBecause of their small size and often delicate structure, bryophytes have a poor fossil record, dating back only about 290 million years."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cba6009a-5cd2-4ade-93fa-2d653a4f259b",
                                                "sense_id": "e7609cd2-202e-38df-a35a-bb737591908b",
                                                "text": "And so it was that I was introduced to Len Ellis and the quiet world of bryophytes – mosses to the rest of us."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
